


TIME(1)             UNIX Programmer's Manual                TIME(1)



NAME
     time - time a command

SYNOPSIS
     time command [ arguments ]

DESCRIPTION
     The given command is executed (searched for along $_P_A_T_H);
     after it is complete, _t_i_m_e prints the elapsed time during
     the command to the standard error stream, in seconds and
     tenths, and exits with the command's exit status.

     This is the 2.11BSD _t_i_m_e adapted to FGX: there is no per-
     process CPU accounting, so only the real (wall-clock) line
     is printed -- the user and sys lines do not exist here.
     Timing uses the 60 Hz system tick counter.

BUGS
     Elapsed time is measured in ticks; anything under a
     sixtieth of a second reads as 0.0.

SEE ALSO
     date(1), sleep(1)

FGX                        2.11BSD port                          1
